From 2ea860845d53107baed7d45f875470b64a676cd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaTor <deltator@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:40:24 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] conflux: add measured-throughput set selection
 (ConfluxSetSelection 4)

Mode 4 measures each set's real delivered download throughput from the
existing per-set bytes_recv counter and spreads new streams in proportion
to it, with a built-in floor of 10% of the fastest set so no set is starved
and every set keeps receiving enough real traffic to stay measurable. The
window is folded lazily when a stream is placed: no timer, no per-cell
accounting, and no extra traffic.

Two new options tune it (0 = internal default):
  - ConfluxProbeInterval: measurement window/re-test period (default 30s)
  - ConfluxProbeMinBytes: minimum delivered bytes per window to trust the
    estimate (default 32768)

Mode 4 bypasses ConfluxSetRttMax/ConfluxSetRttPct so every set is sampled.
